Overlay patch 0048: THE PHYSICAL BLADE (VR R5, VR-DONOR-MAP 8 layer 1).

R4's honest headline gap, recorded in docs/VR-R4-NOTES.md 5.1 and in STATUS.md:
"damage lands along Link's AUTHORED sword arc, not where your hand is." This
patch closes it, and it is the reason R5 exists.

TWO NEW FILES' WORTH OF WORK, ONE NEW FILE. `soh/src/code/z_soh_vr_blade.c` is
added whole (soh/CMakeLists.txt already GLOB_RECURSEs "src/*.c", so it needs no
build-system change), and z_player.c gains exactly two call sites plus their
declarations. Everything in the new file is `#ifdef __IOS__`, so a desktop or
oracle build compiles an empty translation unit.

THE THREE FLOWS AND THEIR TICK ORDERING -- the part that is easy to get wrong
and impossible to debug afterwards:

  HARVEST, at DRAW. The scene's static CollisionPoly list is walked, AABB-culled
  to 20 units around the blade line, back-face rejected at 4 units (a face the
  blade is deeply BEHIND belongs to another volume -- the outside of this wall,
  the ceiling of the room below -- and pushing off it drives the blade the wrong
  way), ranked by TRUE segment-to-triangle distance with a 0.5x sticky bonus for
  polys that already constrain the blade. The donor is explicit (VrSwing.cpp
  :476-497) that CENTROID ranking made big wall triangles lose to small
  irrelevant ones and churned the set every tick, and that stickiness is one of
  three co-required tricks -- a member blinking out for a single step lets the
  sim sink and the snap back IS the jitter. Top 16 published; the shell converts
  to tracking metres every compositor frame and steps the solver against them.

  DAMAGE, at DRAW. Two kinds of AT quad, both vanilla vertex order, both
  TOUCH_NEAREST, both on a collider that is a byte-for-byte mirror of vanilla's
  own D_80854650:
    - the SWEPT quad, corners = the blade's previous and current base and tip.
      This is the quad that makes damage follow the hand, and it is registered
      only while the swing is HOT.
    - the STRIKE quad (donor :1283-1297): an 18x18 square poked 6 units INSIDE
      the surface at each contact the solver reported. It exists BECAUSE the
      blade now physically halts at a surface -- a halted blade's swept quad
      only grazes what it stopped on.
  Damage class comes from the donor's kDmgFlags table mirroring vanilla's
  D_80854488, column 1 (jump-slash, roughly 2x in every enemy's authored table)
  above the heavy-swing speed. So every enemy's own damage table and
  vulnerability set keeps working with nothing re-implemented -- which is the
  same reason R4's sUseHeldItem path was worth having.

  HIT READBACK, at UPDATE, ONE TICK LATE and that is not a bug. Quads are
  registered at draw on tick N; CollisionCheck_AT runs at the top of tick N+1;
  AT_HIT is read then. On a hit gSohVRBladeHitSeq bumps and the shell drops the
  swing tier HOT -> ARMED. That is the donor's ENTIRE "one strike per swing"
  mechanism (VrSwing.cpp:1522-1530): to strike again the blade must re-cross the
  hit speed, which is what a second swing is. No hit list, nothing to leak
  across a scene change, nothing to reset.

WHY THE UPDATE HOOK IS AT THE TOP OF Player_UpdateCommon. The donor records the
ordering trap it cost them (VrSwing.cpp:263-268): CollisionCheck_ResetDamage
zeroes every actor's colChkInfo.displacement at the top of the tick, so anything
written at draw time is wiped before the victim consumes it, and the player
updates BEFORE enemies. We queue nothing at draw that an enemy must consume
(knockback is not ported -- the donor ships it at 0 anyway), but the AT readback
has the same shape and belongs in the same place.

WHAT IS NOT PORTED, listed rather than hidden (docs/VR-R5-NOTES.md carries the
full list): bone capsules and limb puppetry -- the donor's own comment settles
it, "Damage is unaffected either way", and with no puppet the donor itself falls
back to pushing AC colliders as solid prims; dynapoly probe rays, so a blade
does not yet stop on a pushed block or an open door; actor colliders as contact
prims, so it does not yet stop on an enemy; knockback, press-push, hit flinch
(all 0 in the donor's own defaults); and the material SFX table.

THE FALLBACK IS NOT REMOVED. `gSohVRBladeDamage == 0` restores R4 exactly -- a
swing sets sUseHeldItem and Link's authored attack runs, animation, combos, stab
lunge and all. It is a setting because some players will prefer the authored
animation, and it is also what runs the moment the shell reports no hands.

GATING. Everything is behind gSohVRMode && gSohVRFpActive && gSohVRMotionHands
&& gSohVRBladeDamage && gSohVRHandValid[swordHand] -- state the flat window, the
3D panel and every iPhone build never set.

