+ * z_soh_vr_blade.c -- SOH_IOS (overlay 0048, VR R5). THE PHYSICAL BLADE.
+ *
+ * VR-DONOR-MAP 8, layer 1. This is our port of the parts of ShinyWindow's
+ * `VrSwing.cpp` that the `gVrPhysVisualMesh=0` path needs: the GAME's own
+ * collision mesh harvested around the blade and handed outward to the shell's
+ * contact solver, and the damage that comes back in.
+ *
+ * WHAT R4 DID, AND WHY THIS REPLACES IT. R4 turned a detected swing into
+ * `sUseHeldItem = true`, which runs Link's entire AUTHORED attack. Everything
+ * about that worked -- animation, combos, the stab lunge, jump-slash, every
+ * enemy's own damage table -- except the one thing that matters in VR: DAMAGE
+ * LANDED ALONG LINK'S AUTHORED ARC, NOT WHERE YOUR HAND WAS. Swing left and
+ * Link still hit whatever he faced. R5 damages from the blade. The R4 path is
+ * kept, whole, behind `gSohVRBladeDamage == 0`, for anyone who prefers the
+ * authored attack (and as the fallback the moment the shell reports no hands).
+ *
+ * THE THREE FLOWS, and the tick ordering each depends on:
+ *
+ *  1. HARVEST (draw time). Walk the scene's static `CollisionPoly` list,
+ *     AABB-culled to 20 units around the blade line, back-face rejected at 4
+ *     units, ranked by TRUE segment-to-triangle distance (donor :480-497 is
+ *     explicit that centroid ranking made big wall triangles lose to small
+ *     irrelevant ones and churned the set every tick), with a 0.5x sticky bonus
+ *     for polys that already constrain the blade. Top 16 published to the
+ *     shell, which converts to tracking metres and steps the solver at HEADSET
+ *     rate against them.
+ *
+ *  2. DAMAGE (draw time). Two kinds of AT quad, both on the vanilla vertex
+ *     order and both `TOUCH_NEAREST`:
+ *       - the SWEPT quad, corners = the blade's previous and current base and
+ *         tip, registered while the swing is HOT. This is the quad that makes
+ *         damage follow the hand.
+ *       - the STRIKE quad, from each contact the solver reported: an 18x18
+ *         square poked 6 units INSIDE the surface at the impact point (donor
+ *         :1283-1297). It exists because the blade now physically HALTS at a
+ *         surface, so the swept quad only grazes what it stopped on.
+ *     Damage class is the donor's `kDmgFlags` table mirroring vanilla's
+ *     `D_80854488`, column 1 (jump-slash, ~2x in every enemy's authored table)
+ *     above the heavy-swing speed. So every enemy's damage table and
+ *     vulnerability set keeps working with nothing re-implemented.
+ *
+ *  3. HIT READBACK (update time, ONE TICK LATE and that is not a bug). Quads
+ *     are registered at draw on tick N; `CollisionCheck_AT` runs at the top of
+ *     tick N+1; we read `AT_HIT` then. On a hit we bump `gSohVRBladeHitSeq`,
+ *     and the shell drops the swing tier HOT -> ARMED. That is the donor's
+ *     entire "one strike per swing" mechanism (VrSwing.cpp:1522-1530): to
+ *     strike again the blade must re-cross the hit speed, which is what a
+ *     second swing IS. No hit list, nothing to leak, nothing to reset.
+ *
+ * NOT PORTED, and listed in docs/VR-R5-NOTES.md rather than hidden: bone
+ * capsules and limb puppetry (the donor's own comment at VrSwing.cpp:499-507
+ * settles it -- "Damage is unaffected either way"), dynapoly probe rays, actor
+ * AC/OC colliders as contact prims, knockback and press-push (which the donor
+ * ships at 0 anyway), and the material SFX table.
+ */
